#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:1
msgid "Release 2.20.0 (2024-01-29)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:3
msgid ""
"Option `allowed-uris` can now match whole schemes in URIs without slashes "
"[\\#9547](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9547)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:5
msgid ""
"If a scheme, such as `github:` is specified in the `allowed-uris` option, "
"all URIs starting with `github:` are allowed. Previously this only worked "
"for schemes whose URIs used the `://` syntax."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:8
msgid ""
"Include cgroup stats when building through the daemon [\\#9598](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9598)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:10
msgid ""
"Nix now also reports cgroup statistics when building through the Nix daemon "
"and when doing remote builds using `ssh-ng`, if both sides of the connection "
"are using Nix 2.20 or newer."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:13
msgid ""
"Disallow empty search regex in `nix search` [\\#9481](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/9481)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:15
msgid ""
"[`nix search`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-search.md) now requires a search "
"regex to be passed. To show all packages, use `^`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:17
msgid ""
"Add new `eval-system` setting [\\#4093](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/4093)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:19
msgid ""
"Add a new `eval-system` option. Unlike `system`, it just overrides the value "
"of `builtins.currentSystem`. This is more useful than overriding `system`, "
"because you can build these derivations on remote builders which can work on "
"the given system. In contrast, `system` also affects scheduling which will "
"cause Nix to build those derivations locally even if that doesn't make sense."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:24
msgid ""
"`eval-system` only takes effect if it is non-empty. If empty (the default) "
"`system` is used as before, so there is no breakage."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:27
msgid ""
"Import-from-derivation builds the derivation in the build store [\\#9661]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9661)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:29
msgid ""
"When using `--eval-store`, `import`ing from a derivation will now result in "
"the derivation being built on the build store, i.e. the store specified in "
"the `store` Nix option."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:31
msgid ""
"Because the resulting Nix expression must be copied back to the evaluation "
"store in order to be imported, this requires the evaluation store to trust "
"the build store's signatures."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:33
msgid ""
"Mounted SSH Store [\\#7890](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/7890) "
"[\\#7912](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/7912)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:35
msgid ""
"Introduced the store [`mounted-ssh-ng://`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-help-"
"stores.md). This store allows full access to a Nix store on a remote machine "
"and additionally requires that the store be mounted in the local filesystem."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:38
msgid ""
"Rename `nix show-config` to `nix config show` [\\#7672](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/issues/7672) [\\#9477](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9477)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:40
msgid ""
"`nix show-config` was renamed to `nix config show`, and `nix doctor` was "
"renamed to `nix config check`, to be more consistent with the rest of the "
"command line interface."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:42
msgid ""
"Add command `nix hash convert` [\\#9452](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/9452)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:44
msgid ""
"This replaces the old `nix hash to-*` commands, which are still available "
"but will emit a deprecation warning. Please convert as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:46
msgid ""
"`nix hash to-base16 $hash1 $hash2`: Use `nix hash convert --to base16 $hash1 "
"$hash2` instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:47
msgid ""
"`nix hash to-base32 $hash1 $hash2`: Use `nix hash convert --to nix32 $hash1 "
"$hash2` instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:48
msgid ""
"`nix hash to-base64 $hash1 $hash2`: Use `nix hash convert --to base64 $hash1 "
"$hash2` instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:49
msgid ""
"`nix hash to-sri $hash1 $hash2`: : Use `nix hash convert --to sri $hash1 "
"$hash2` or even just `nix hash convert $hash1 $hash2` instead."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:51
msgid ""
"Rename hash format `base32` to `nix32` [\\#9452](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/9452)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:53
msgid ""
"Hash format `base32` was renamed to `nix32` since it used a special Nix-"
"specific character set for [Base32](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Base32)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:56
msgid ""
"`nix profile` now allows referring to elements by human-readable names "
"[\\#8678](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/8678)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:58
msgid ""
"[`nix profile`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile.md) now uses names to "
"refer to installed packages when running [`list`](../command-ref/new-cli/"
"nix3-profile-list.md), [`remove`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile-remove."
"md) or [`upgrade`](../command-ref/new-cli/nix3-profile-upgrade.md) as "
"opposed to indices. Profile element names are generated when a package is "
"installed and remain the same until the package is removed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:60
msgid ""
"**Warning**: The `manifest.nix` file used to record the contents of profiles "
"has changed. Nix will automatically upgrade profiles to the new version when "
"you modify the profile. After that, the profile can no longer be used by "
"older versions of Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:62
msgid ""
"Give `nix store add` a `--hash-algo` flag [\\#9809](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/pull/9809)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:64
msgid ""
"Adds a missing feature that was present in the old CLI, and matches our "
"plans to have similar flags for `nix hash convert` and `nix hash path`."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:67
msgid "Coercion errors include the failing value"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:69
msgid ""
"The `error: cannot coerce a <TYPE> to a string` message now includes the "
"value which caused the error."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:72 source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:93
msgid "Before:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:78 source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:99
msgid "After:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:88
msgid "Type errors include the failing value"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:90
msgid ""
"In errors like `value is an integer while a list was expected`, the message "
"now includes the failing value."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:108
msgid ""
"Source locations are printed more consistently in errors [\\#561](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/561) [\\#9555](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/9555)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:110
msgid ""
"Source location information is now included in error messages more "
"consistently. Given this code:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:113
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"let\n"
"  attr = {foo = \"bar\";};\n"
"  key = {};\n"
"in\n"
"  attr.${key}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:121
msgid ""
"Previously, Nix would show this unhelpful message when attempting to "
"evaluate it:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:131
msgid "Now, the error message displays where the problematic value was found:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:147
msgid ""
"Some stack overflow segfaults are fixed [\\#9616](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/issues/9616) [\\#9617](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9617)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:149
msgid ""
"The number of nested function calls has been restricted, to detect and "
"report infinite function call recursions. The default maximum call depth is "
"10,000 and can be set with [the `max-call-depth` option](../command-ref/conf-"
"file.md#conf-max-call-depth)."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:154
msgid ""
"This replaces the `stack overflow (possible infinite recursion)` message."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:156
msgid ""
"Better error reporting for `with` expressions [\\#9658](https://github.com/"
"NixOS/nix/pull/9658)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:158
msgid ""
"`with` expressions using non-attrset values to resolve variables are now "
"reported with proper positions, e.g."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:171
msgid ""
"Functions are printed with more detail [\\#7145](https://github.com/NixOS/"
"nix/issues/7145) [\\#9606](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9606)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:173
msgid ""
"`nix repl`, `nix eval`, `builtins.trace`, and most other places values are "
"printed will now include function names and source location information:"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:176
msgid ""
"```\n"
"$ nix repl nixpkgs\n"
"nix-repl> builtins.map\n"
"«primop map»\n"
"\n"
"nix-repl> builtins.map lib.id\n"
"«partially applied primop map»\n"
"\n"
"nix-repl> builtins.trace lib.id \"my-value\"\n"
"trace: «lambda id @ /nix/store/kgr5lnaiiv08wb7k324yv1i1npjmrvjc-source/lib/"
"trivial.nix:26:5»\n"
"\"my-value\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:189
msgid ""
"Flake operations like `nix develop` will no longer fail when run in a Git "
"repository where the `flake.lock` file is `.gitignore`d [\\#8854](https://"
"github.com/NixOS/nix/issues/8854) [\\#9324](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"pull/9324)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:194
msgid ""
"Nix commands will now respect Ctrl-C [\\#7145](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/"
"issues/7145) [\\#6995](https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/6995) [\\#9687]"
"(https://github.com/NixOS/nix/pull/9687)"
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:199
msgid ""
"Previously, many Nix commands would hang indefinitely if Ctrl-C was pressed "
"while performing various operations (including `nix develop`, `nix flake "
"update`, and so on). With several fixes to Nix's signal handlers, Nix "
"commands will now exit quickly after Ctrl-C is pressed."
msgstr ""

#: source/release-notes/rl-2.20.md:204
msgid ""
"`nix copy` to a `ssh-ng` store now needs `--substitute-on-destination` (a.k."
"a. `-s`) in order to substitute paths on the remote store instead of copying "
"them. The behavior is consistent with `nix copy` to a different kind of "
"remote store. Previously this behavior was controlled by the `builders-use-"
"substitutes` setting and `--substitute-on-destination` was ignored."
msgstr ""
